<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 72,830 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 72,830 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-01-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 72,830 tonnes of export and import cargo in 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Tuesday compared to 79,711 tonnes in the same period on Monday.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>				    Tuesday     Jan 6</p>
<p>    Export cargo		19,549	 7,673</p>
<p>    Import cargo		53,281	72,038</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, six ships sailed and two berthed. In the next 24 hours, four are expected to sail and nine are expected to arrive.  </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at Karachi Port:</p>
<p>    Commodity	  Tonnes/TEUs  Ship		   Berthing</p>
<p>Fuel oil		 40,000	 Trade Resolve	7/1</p>
<p>Fertiliser	     24,657	 Danakos-1	    8/1</p>
<p>Crude oil		68,000	 Stavros-1	    9/1</p>
<p>High speed diesel    75,000	 Chesapeak City    11/1</p>
<p>Fertiliser	     21,316	 Evelyn		11/1</p>
<p>Containers		  600	 Contship Asia     15/1</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
